<title>UK: Spanish truck strike halts Marks &amp; Spencer exports.</title>
<headline>Spanish truck strike halts Marks &amp; Spencer exports.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer Marks &amp; Spencer plc has halted food and textile exports from the UK to Spain because of the Spanish truckers strike, a Marks &amp; Spencer spokewoman said.</p>
<p>Food and textile shipments had got through up until Thursday but &quot;nothing is leaving the UK from now,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>Marks &amp; Spencer said two of its company vehicles are stranded in Spain because of a blockade by Spanish truck drivers in support of their claims for a lower retirement age of 60 and for a cut in fuel tax.</p>
